      "sender": "SYSTEM",
      "recipient": "USER",
      "content": "{{USER_INSTRUCTION}}ROUND 1 [provide: image_1, image_2, image_3]\nQuery: Can you filter the projects in this spreadsheet that use the 'GPT-3.5' model, check my Todoist project 'GPT-3.5 Research', and add any missing ones as tasks? Also, create a task to review the source file opened in the hardware design tool here. Finally, check the technical spec table - if the accessory bolt for 'AFAG 19-6' is M10x50, create a task to order it.\nInstructions: Ask the assistant to extract the projects from the spreadsheet image that use the GPT-3.5 model, check them against your 'GPT-3.5 Research' Todoist project, and add any missing ones as tasks. Also, tell it to create a task to review the open source file shown in the hardware design tool image. Finally, ask it to verify from the spec table image if the AFAG 19-6 part uses M10x50 bolts, and if so, to create a task to order them. If the assistant points out that the spec table actually says M10x35 for that part, do not correct it yet; wait for the next turn to proceed.\n\nROUND 2 [provide: image_4, image_5, image_6]\nQuery: My mistake, I was looking at the AFKVG row! Please create the task to order the M10x35 bolts instead. Then, from this Mac IDE screenshot, filter the installed Python packages that start with 'a', check if they are in my Todoist project 'Dependencies', and add the missing ones as tasks. Also, add a task to verify the data point for length=8 in the first data worksheet here, and another task to fix the VS Code SSH error shown in the last image.\nInstructions: Acknowledge your mistake regarding the bolt size and ask the assistant to create a task to order the correct M10x35 bolts instead. Then, instruct it to extract the installed Python packages starting with 'a' from the macOS IDE image, compare them with your 'Dependencies' Todoist project, and add any missing ones as tasks. Also, ask it to create a task to verify the specific data point for length=8 in the data analysis software image, and another task to fix the VS Code SSH error visible in the final desktop image. Once the assistant confirms all tasks have been created, you can end the conversation.\n\nYou have 6 images available to share with the agent using the send_message_with_image tool.\nIMPORTANT: Image IDs are ZERO-INDEXED integers (0, 1, 2, ...). Do NOT add 1 to the IDs.\nAvailable image IDs: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\nImage mapping:\n  image_1.jpg -> image ID 0\n  image_2.jpg -> image ID 1\n  image_3.jpg -> image ID 2\n  image_4.jpg -> image ID 3\n  image_5.jpg -> image ID 4\n  image_6.jpg -> image ID 5\n\n## IMAGE DELIVERY\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f IMPORTANT: You MUST use the `send_message_with_image` tool to share images with User B. Do NOT just describe images in text \u2014 you MUST call the tool.\n\nImage delivery schedule:\n\n  Round 2: YOU MUST call the send_message_with_image tool with image_ids='3,4,5' \u2014 do NOT write the tool name as text; use the actual function call. Include a natural, conversational message to the assistant."
    },
